 # License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this
 # file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
 
+# Upstream this file declares the whole application-update machinery. In this
+# tree it declares none of it: the updater, the MAR signature checks, the MAR
+# channel identifiers, the maintenance service, the update agent and the binary
+# patch formats were removed on 2026-08-31 on the owner's instruction - "tutto
+# quello che riguarda aggiornamenti", and explicitly NOT as a --disable-updater
+# lever, so that nothing is left to switch back on.
+#
+# The consequence is deliberate and is recorded in the workbench docs
+# (27-retail-network-parity.md): MOZ_UPDATER is never set, so
+# toolkit/mozapps/update is not built, AppConstants.MOZ_UPDATER is false, every
+# #ifdef MOZ_UPDATER compiles out, no updater binary is packaged, and the
+# browser never contacts aus5.mozilla.org. The "Update available" badge that
+# UpdateListener shows unconditionally therefore has no code left to show it.
+#
+# What did NOT go, because it is not update machinery: --enable-update-channel
+# (MOZ_UPDATE_CHANNEL). That option names the CHANNEL, and RemotingName is
+# derived from it - `firefox` on release, `firefox-default` without it - so
+# removing it would rename the application on disk and on the wire.
+#
+# Two options that upstream keeps in this file are unrelated to updates and are
+# kept: the default browser agent and the notification server.
+#
+# Since 157 a third one is kept for the same reason: the macOS dmgInstallHelper
+# debug option (also unrelated to updates).
 
 # dmgInstallHelper
 # ==============================================================
